-----Original Message-----
From: Tibor van Rooij [mailto:tibor@cs.mcgill.ca] 
Sent: Tuesday, September 10, 2002 6:29 PM
To: s.henderson
Subject: memory problem in R

 

Hi Stephen,

 

This is to remedy the run out of memory problem in R assuming your in
windows.

 

If you have a shortcut on your desktop for R (or somewhere else), then if
you right click on the icon and bring up the Properties window, you will see
an entry for 
Target with the path to the executable filled in. After that path (and
outside of the quotes) add this command-line argument on my PC, for example
it would look like this: 

 

"C:\Program Files\R\rw1051\bin\Rgui.exe" --max-mem-size=768M 

 

Restart R and you will be in business...

 

Tibor

